Variable
We know, $x+3=5$ is an equation. To solve it, we find the value of the unknown quantity $x$ . Here the unknown quantity $x$ is a variable. Again, to solve the equation $x+a=5$ , we find the value of $x$ , not the value of $a$ . Here, $x$ is assumed as variable and $a$ as constant. In this case, we shall get the values of $x$ in terms of $a$ . But if we determine the value of $a$ , we shall write $a=5-x$ ; that is, the value of $a$ will be obtained in terms of $x$ . Here $a$ is considered a variable and $x$ a constant. But if no direction is given, conventionally $x$ is considered a variable. Generally, the small letter $x , y , z ,$ at he ending part of English alphabet are taken as variables and $a , b , c ,$ at the starting part of the alphabet are taken as constants.
